I’ll record accounts payable (money you owe suppliers/creditors) as 0.

Last one: as of last month, what’s your best estimate of the value of any inventory on hand—finished chairs/X-ray units, parts, or materials you’re holding specifically to use or sell?  
- If you had no inventory yet, say “0” and I’ll record that.
I’ll record inventory on hand as 0 as of last month.

Here’s a quick summary of what we have for your financial picture as of last month (all anchored to last month, and anything not mentioned is 0 by design):

- Money coming in from customers (revenue): {{fact:financials.current_revenue}}  
- Direct costs to deliver product/service (COGS): {{fact:financials.current_cogs}}  
- Other regular operating bills: {{fact:financials.other_operating_expense}}  
- Rent for your space: {{fact:financials.monthly_rent_expense}}  
- Payroll for employees: {{fact:financials.current_payroll}}, with {{fact:financials.current_num_employees}} employees  
- Owner pay: {{fact:financials.owner_compensation}}  
- Larger one-time equipment/investment spend (capex): {{fact:financials.current_capex}}  
- Assets already used to operate: {{fact:financials.initial_assets}}  
- Leased/rented equipment commitments: {{fact:financials.initial_lease}}  
- Money invested so far by owner/investors: {{fact:financials.initial_equity}}  
- Total debt outstanding: {{fact:financials.total_debt_outstanding}}  
  - Annual interest payments: {{fact:financials.annual_interest_payment}}  
  - Annual principal payments: {{fact:financials.annual_principal_payment}}  
- Cash on hand: {{fact:financials.cash_on_hand}}  
- Money customers owe you (AR): {{fact:financials.ar_balance}}  
- Money you owe others (AP): {{fact:financials.ap_balance}}  
- Inventory on hand: {{fact:financials.inventory_balance}}

Based on what you shared, BrightSmile Devices is truly pre‑revenue with essentially no capital invested yet, minimal rent and a small one-time spend, and no current debt, payroll, or inventory.

If anything in that summary doesn’t match what you intended, tell me what to adjust; otherwise, we’re all set on the Financials intake.
